WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.613
Okay, our first question is coming from Cammy.

2
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.890
What is your question to Damona?

3
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:10.470
I'm 45, I am single and I am so old-school,

4
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.940
where I am not approaching any man.

5
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.860
I can be in a party and we will just have a staring match

6
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.730 line:15%
and then we both go home.

7
00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.790 line:15%
What advice or what tips can you give me, Damona

8
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:24.330
on how to break out of that shell and just go for it?

9
00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.240
How, how, how?

10
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.350
Cammy, you're an old-school girl

11
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.760
living in a new-school world.

12
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.100
Okay?
(audience laughing)

13
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.760
So, I want to just set aside those beliefs

14
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.410
that were probably passed down to you

15
00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:38.847
from generation to generation.

16
00:00:38.847 --> 00:00:40.210
"This is how it's done."

17
00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:41.920
We're in a complete different paradigm.

18
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.319
And just starting a conversation with someone,

19
00:00:44.319 --> 00:00:48.200
that is not a marriage, that is not a marriage proposal,

20
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.850
that is not a commitment.

21
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.340
That's just a conversation

22
00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:52.730
and you never know where it's going to go.

23
00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:55.730
So, I really want you to reframe any thinking

24
00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.390
around it being a rejection.

25
00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.390
So I actually, I would give you a little assignment.

26
00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:03.890
Okay.
To be a little bit brave.

27
00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.750
And the next time you're making eyes at someone,

28
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:09.610
go ahead and initiate the conversation and see what happens.

29
00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.650
'Cause the more you do that, Cammy,

30
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:15.810 line:15%
the less weight you'll put on each individual interaction

31
00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:19.400 line:15%
and the less anxiety and worry that will come up

32
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.630 line:15%
when you go to talk to someone the next time.

33
00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.275 line:15%
Practice makes perfect, right?

34
00:01:23.275 --> 00:01:25.530
Exactly. You got it.
Let me get my practice.

35
00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.869
Thank you. Thank you.
(audience applauding)

36
00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:28.702
I agree.

37
00:01:28.702 --> 00:01:29.950
I agree with that a lot.

38
00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.900
Also, I really am having like a kind of, "Ah-ha" moment,

39
00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.830
because I am Josie Grossie

40
00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.410
and I think that everybody can feel that.

41
00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.260
So when I go up to talk to a guy,

42
00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:40.865
here's what's happening on the inside.

43
00:01:40.865 --> 00:01:43.873
(Drew exclaims loudly) Hi.
(audience laughing)

44
00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.810
But I think all they see is, "Hey, what's going on?"

45
00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.900
But they can't tell what is happening on the inside.

46
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.260
But we think it's all out there.

47
00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.730
And he's Josie Grossie on the inside too.

48
00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:57.930
That's the crazy thing.

49
00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:58.820
Is he really?

50
00:01:58.820 --> 00:01:59.653
Yeah.

51
00:01:59.653 --> 00:02:01.449
I mean like, Joseph Grossie.
(laughs loudly)

52
00:02:01.449 --> 00:02:02.730
Joseph Grossie!

53
00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:03.780
Oh, my gosh!

54
00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.090
Damona, I am looking for my Joseph Grossie.

55
00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.523
He's out there.

56
00:02:08.523 --> 00:02:10.580
(both laughing)
(audience laughing)

57
00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.747
(audience applauding)

58
00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.490
Okay, our next question is coming from Linda.

59
00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:20.880
Linda, what is your question for Damona?

60
00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.230
Hi, Drew. Hi, Damona.

61
00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.390
I need help.

62
00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:25.223
Okay.

63
00:02:25.223 --> 00:02:29.290
I've been on and off dating apps for the past two years.

64
00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.363
I'm middle-aged and I would like to settle down.

65
00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.730
The last date that I went on,

66
00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.200
the guy showed up looking 25 years older

67
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.340
than his profile picture.

68
00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.740 line:15%
He lied about his profession.

69
00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:42.920 line:15%
He said he was a doctor

70
00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.342 line:15%
and he showed up with a stethoscope in his pocket.

71
00:02:45.342 --> 00:02:46.890 line:15%
(audience laughs softly)

72
00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.190 line:15%
And he lived in his office.

73
00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:52.370 line:15%
So my question is, how do I get better

74
00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.910
at pre-screening and screening,

75
00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.593
so I don't get catfished again?

76
00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.270
I love this question.

77
00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:03.290
Well, first of all, Linda, it's not in your head.

78
00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.290
There's two categories of catfish.

79
00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:06.390
There are the people

80
00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.790
who aren't really confident in who they are,

81
00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.510
which is what you were dealing with.

82
00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:14.340
And the people who are, have nefarious intentions.

83
00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.620
Who, you know, want to scam you and take your money.

84
00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:20.420
So, I guess the positive side is that

85
00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:21.910
we didn't have that kind of catfish,

86
00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.860
but the negative side is it's just as, it's disappointing.

87
00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.730
You've invested time and you had, you know, a hope

88
00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.890
that this person was going to be who they said they were.

89
00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:32.883
So, here's what I want you to look out for next time.

90
00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:37.260
On the photos they have to be,

91
00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.560
they have to seem current.

92
00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.130 line:15%
If they're not crisp digital quality...

93
00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:44.840 line:15%
Like, we're all carrying high-quality cameras

94
00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.750 line:15%
in our pockets every day.

95
00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:50.250 line:15%
There is no excuse for having like, a scanned photo

96
00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.270 line:15%
or something that looks like it's too far away

97
00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.320 line:15%
or isn't really clear.

98
00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.500 line:15%
And you can always ask for more photos

99
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.010 line:15%
if you're not really sure.

100
00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:01.177
Also in those photos, if they look posed,

101
00:04:01.177 --> 00:04:03.070
and I'm not talking about like, posed.

102
00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.937
I'm talking about like, brochure level posed.

103
00:04:05.937 --> 00:04:08.420
(Drew laughs)
That is a really big sign.

104
00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.950
And especially if they're in a uniform.

105
00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.070
Like, you'll see this a lot of times with doctors,

106
00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:17.070
with people in the armed services.

107
00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.770
So, look out for those things.

108
00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:21.267
If you're spidey senses go off and you feel like,

109
00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:23.410
"Oh, I don't know about this picture",

110
00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.750
go and run it through a Google image search.

111
00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:26.970
Do you know how to do this?
Yup.

112
00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:28.790
Just in Google, you can go into the search bar.

113
00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:32.040
You can go up to image and you can search a photo

114
00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.690
and see if it comes up associated with anything else.

115
00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:38.550
Anything that doesn't match with what they've told you.

116
00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.450
That's how I found out he wasn't a doctor.

117
00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:41.283
Well, there you go.

118
00:04:41.283 --> 00:04:44.030
So you wanna do that before you get invested

119
00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:47.850
and before you actually meet up with this person.

120
00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.900
Another sign is that they'll love bomb you.

121
00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.760
They'll tell you all of the things that you wanna hear.

122
00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:57.460
They'll whisper sweet nothings into your inbox.

123
00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.090
And then they,

124
00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:02.480
if you step back and you read what they've said,

125
00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.640
you realize it could kind of be said to anybody.

126
00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.900
It might not be that specific.

127
00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:12.290
That could be a sign of the other kind of catfish.

128
00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:16.380
Also, if those people don't want to meet up in person

129
00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.400
or won't at least do a video date.

130
00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.540
Now, that is a primary screening to get to the date,

131
00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.170
to do a video chat date.

132
00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:26.730
And if they seem squirrelly about that

133
00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:28.780
there's definitely something going on.

134
00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.600
Linda, what do you think?

135
00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.180
Definitely helpful.

136
00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.800
I don't know why I didn't think of it myself.

137
00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.051
Yeah.
Exactly.

138
00:05:36.051 --> 00:05:39.218
(audience applauding)

139
00:05:41.446 --> 00:05:43.140
And you are so stunning.

140
00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:43.973
Thank you.

141
00:05:43.973 --> 00:05:47.250
Like, you are the catch and I can see this about you.

142
00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:49.550
And it's funny, when it comes to ourselves

143
00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:53.020
all of a sudden we don't have that same sort of

144
00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:55.610
fierce loyalty of protection.

145
00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:58.320
So, you are so worth it.

146
00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.040
You are so beautiful inside and out and you are not alone.

147
00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.563
I swear I've gone through the same exact things.

148
00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.830
Just elusiveness, too much mystery,

149
00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:10.430
I don't know where I stand,

150
00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:11.810
I don't know who I'm dealing with.

151
00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:14.380
I totally have dealt with the same thing on dating apps.

152
00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.939
So, let's try and figure this out.

153
00:06:15.939 --> 00:06:17.838
(audience applauding)

154
00:06:17.838 --> 00:06:19.572
'Cause it's not changing.

155
00:06:19.572 --> 00:06:22.155 line:15%
(upbeat music)

